diff --git a/wiki/log.d/20260825-000000-daemon-auto-retry.md b/wiki/log.d/20260825-000000-daemon-auto-retry.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..bf8a3d3c3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/wiki/log.d/20260825-000000-daemon-auto-retry.md
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+---
+created: 2026-08-25
+tags: [daemon, auto-retry, recovery]
+---
+
+**Feature:** Daemon auto-retry for recoverable terminal error markers.
+
+**Problem:** When the daemon parked a task on a terminal `ERROR` marker
+because an external dependency was temporarily broken (codex auth 401 on
+`implementer_failed`; stale claude launcher/tmux on
+`claude_launch_failed`), the task stayed red forever even after the
+dependency healed. Recovery required a manual `hive markers clear`
+(observed live with task-58-style codex 401s and task-287-style
+claude-launch failures).
+
+**Action:** New `Hive::Daemon::AutoRetry::*` modules wired into the
+dispatcher tick after the stale-agent healer:
+
+1. **Classifier (U1)** — closed v1 allowlist with REQUIRED diagnostic
+   signatures matched over the marker `message=` attr plus
+   `diagnostics/red-status.md` / newest log tail: `implementer_failed`
+   only as codex 401/missing-bearer/basic-auth;
+   `claude_launch_failed` only with launcher/wrapper/readiness text.
+   Everything else stays manual.
+2. **ProbeRunner (U2)** — per-probe hard timeouts (10–30s), process-group
+   kill at the deadline, verbatim output capture, tick-scoped caching;
+   hang/error/nonzero ⇒ not healthy.
+3. **Concrete probes (U3)** — in-process real `hive doctor` universal
+   precondition; codex auth (`login status` logged-in AND tiny
+   `codex exec` smoke, both in the daemon's own env); claude launcher
+   (`--version` wrapper check + tmux readiness detector).
+4. **Engine (U4/U6/U7)** — fingerprint-gated re-probing (stat-only hash of
+   binaries/wrapper mtimes/config/env/skill dirs + 30-min fallback),
+   2-attempts-per-task-per-reason cap with immediate→30-min backoff and a
+   one-shot `parked_exhausted` terminal event, marker-id-guarded clear via
+   the same locked primitive `hive markers clear` uses, rerun enqueued as
+   a normal `hive run <slug> --project <project>` dispatch request
+   (`requestor=healer`, `trigger=auto_retry`), and dual-channel audit:
+   `auto_retry_decision` daemon-log event plus an `auto_retry_decision`
+   record in the task's `events.jsonl`. Negative decisions throttle to
+   once per fingerprint change/fallback window.
+5. **SafetyGuard (U5)** — default-deny work-area guard reusing the
+   existing `review.fix.auto_commit.scope_check` glob knowledge for the
+   execute stage; answered brainstorm content or non-empty plan.md always
+   blocks; terminal success markers never retry.
+6. **Config (U8)** — `daemon.auto_retry.enabled`, default `true`,
+   strict-boolean validated; `false` is a zero-cost early return.
+
+Attempt bookkeeping persists at `<state_home>/daemon_auto_retry_state.json`
+(atomic write, fail-closed load) so budgets survive daemon restarts.
+
+**Tests:** `test/unit/daemon/auto_retry/` — classifier signature matrix,
+probe timeout/error/caching behavior, probe composition (doctor-red fails
+everything), safety-guard default-deny cases, multi-tick engine sequences
+(retry/backoff/exhaustion, fingerprint gating, throttled negatives,
+kill-switch early return, live-lock skips), and kill-switch config
+validation.
