@@ -0,0 +1,71 @@
+---
+title: Hive::Daemon::AutoRetry
+type: module
+source: lib/hive/daemon/auto_retry/
+created: 2026-08-25
+updated: 2026-08-25
+tags: [daemon, module, auto-retry, recovery, markers]
+---
+
+**TLDR**: Conservative daemon-side auto-recovery for parked tasks whose
+terminal `ERROR` marker was caused by a temporarily-broken EXTERNAL
+dependency. A closed v1 allowlist (`implementer_failed` with the codex
+401/missing-auth signature; `claude_launch_failed` with the
+launcher/wrapper/readiness signature) is gated on health probes
+(`hive doctor` + reason-specific CLI probes), a default-deny work-area
+safety guard, fingerprint-gated re-probing, and a hard 2-attempts-per-
+task-per-reason cap with immediate→30-minute backoff. Retry mechanics are
+byte-for-byte manual-clear equivalence: the same locked
+`Hive::Markers.clear_current` primitive `hive markers clear` uses, then a
+`hive run <slug> --project <project>` dispatch request through the normal
+queue. Kill-switch: `daemon.auto_retry.enabled: false` (default `true`).
+
+## Module map
+
+| Piece | File | Purpose |
+|-------|------|---------|
+| Classifier | `lib/hive/daemon/auto_retry/classify.rb` | Pure allowlist + diagnostic-signature match over the marker's `message=` attr plus `diagnostics/red-status.md` / newest task log tail. Anything unmatched stays parked (AE3). |
+| ProbeRunner | `lib/hive/daemon/auto_retry/probes.rb` | Uniform probe execution: hard per-command timeouts (10–30s), pgroup kill on deadline, verbatim stdout/stderr capture, tick-scoped result cache (one runner per engine tick). Hang/error/nonzero ⇒ not healthy (AE6). |
+| HealthProbes | `lib/hive/daemon/auto_retry/health_probes*.rb` | Universal in-process `hive doctor` precondition + codex auth probe (`codex login status` must be logged-in AND tiny `codex exec` smoke succeeds) + claude launcher probe (`claude --version` wrapper check + tmux readiness detector). Doctor red fails every composition. |
+| Fingerprint | `lib/hive/daemon/auto_retry/fingerprint.rb` | Cheap stat-only health-signal hash: daemon binary, agent binaries/wrapper mtimes, relevant config blocks, inherited env slice, skill-inventory dir mtimes. State-only signals (e.g. codex logout without file change) are covered by the 30-min fallback re-probe. |
+| SafetyGuard | `lib/hive/daemon/auto_retry/safety.rb` | Default-deny: execute stage needs a clean worktree or only paths passing the existing `review.fix.auto_commit.scope_check` globs; brainstorm with any answered question is unsafe; non-empty `plan.md` unsafe; terminal success markers always block; unknown stage/refusal ⇒ no retry (AE5). |
+| StateStore | `lib/hive/daemon/auto_retry/state_store.rb` | Crash-safe JSON bookkeeping at `<state_home>/daemon_auto_retry_state.json`, keyed `[project, slug, stage, reason]`: attempts, last fingerprint, last attempt/probe/negative times, exhausted flag. Atomic write, fail-closed load. |
+| Engine | `lib/hive/daemon/auto_retry/engine.rb` | The tick decision loop (wired into `Dispatcher#tick` after the stale-agent healer): classify → skip exhausted → exhaust on attempts ≥ 2 → fingerprint gate → probes → backoff gate → safety → clear+enqueue → dual-channel audit (`auto_retry_decision` daemon-log event AND `auto_retry_decision` event in the task's `events.jsonl`). Negative decisions throttle to once per fingerprint change or fallback interval. |
+
+## Decision flow per parked row
+
+1. Skip legacy-layout projects, live controller slots, live task locks,
+   non-`error` markers.
+2. Classify (U1); non-recoverable never enters evaluation.
+3. `exhausted` ⇒ silent permanent park; `attempts >= 2` ⇒ mark exhausted +
+   one-shot `parked_exhausted` audit event.
+4. Probe only when the health-signal fingerprint changed since the last
+   probe OR ≥ 30 min elapsed (fallback).
+5. Healthy? No ⇒ throttled negative decision. Yes but < 30 min since retry
+   #1 ⇒ throttled negative. Yes and safety guard denies ⇒ throttled
+   negative with rationale.
+6. Otherwise: marker-id-guarded `clear_current`, enqueue
+   `hive run <slug> --project <project>` (`requestor=healer`,
+   `trigger=auto_retry`) so caps/cooldown/in-flight gates still apply, bump
+   attempts, audit `retried`. If the enqueue write fails AFTER the clear,
+   the audit action is `retry_enqueue_failed` with the exact manual rerun
+   command.
+
+## Config
+
+```yaml
+daemon:
+  auto_retry:
+    enabled: true   # global kill-switch; false = zero probes, zero events
+```
+
+Strict boolean validation in `Config.validate_daemon!` (repo convention);
+a disabled engine logs one `auto_retry_disabled` event at dispatcher
+construction and costs nothing per tick.
